course: dictionary
lesson: 2828
title: One word, three meanings: dividend
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. In a maths sum, the dividend is the number you start with. In 12 ÷ 3 = 4, the dividend is 12, because 12 is the number being divided.
explain: In money lessons, a dividend is a share of a company's profit paid to people who own shares in it. In everyday talk, «hard work will pay dividends» means good results will come later. Check the clues: a division sum means maths, shares or profit mean money, and «pay dividends» means a reward that comes later.
explain: The liar's dividend is a harder example: «The liar's dividend means people use the existence of fakes to deny things that really happened.» Here it is a name for a trick. Someone says something real is fake, because people know fakes exist. Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: In maths, the dividend is the number being divided, so in 20 ÷ 4 = 5 the dividend is 20.
fact: The divisor is the number you divide by, and the quotient is the answer: dividend ÷ divisor = quotient.
fact: In money, «dividend» means a share of a company's profit paid to people who own shares in it.
fact: «Pay dividends» means a benefit or reward that comes later from something you did.
fact: «The liar's dividend» means people use the existence of fakes to deny things that really happened.
exercise: In 20 ÷ 4 = 5, which number is the dividend? | 5 | *20 | 4
exercise: What is a dividend when you own shares in a company? | *A share of the company's profit paid to you | A list of all the shares the company sells | A price you pay to buy the shares
exercise: «Hard work will pay dividends» means | Your money will be taken away | *Good results will come later | You will get tired today
test: In the sum 45 ÷ 9 = 5, what is the dividend? | 9 | 5 | 36 | *45
test: «The liar's dividend means people use the existence of fakes to deny things that really happened.» What does this sentence describe? | *Someone calling a real thing fake because fakes exist | A sum where you divide money between friends | A liar who always tells the truth
exam: Which sentence uses «dividend» to mean a reward that comes later? | The dividend in 18 ÷ 6 = 3 is 18 | Shareholders received a dividend of ten pounds | *Her daily practice will pay dividends when the team plays in the final | Divide the apples between the three children
